+/** \brief Frees the memory blocks that hold no allocation, in the default pools and in every custom pool, down to the minimum block count of each.
+
+The allocator keeps one empty block of each memory type once its allocations are freed, so that the next allocation does not create a block again.
+This function gives that memory back, such as some time after a burst of allocations or when the system reports that its memory is low.
+*/
